  "body": "## Description\nThis bug exists in the `_matchIncomingOrder` [function](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/9f06332ebd4cfe2577d9eae81aeb58d3662ffccd/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L823-L827) in `CLOB.sol` where quote-denominated fill orders (`amountIsBase: false`) incorrectly track remaining amounts when lot-size flooring occurs.\n\n\nThe issue is in the `matchedAmount` [calculation logic](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/9f06332ebd4cfe2577d9eae81aeb58d3662ffccd/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L823-L827)\n\nWhen `baseDelta != matchedBase` (which happens when lot-size flooring reduces the tradeable amount), the system incorrectly sets `matchedAmount = takerOrder.amount` (the full remaining quote amount) instead of `quoteDelta` (the actual quote amount consumed).\n\nThe incorrect `matchedAmount` is used to decrement the incoming order's remaining amount in both [bid](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/9f06332ebd4cfe2577d9eae81aeb58d3662ffccd/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L763) and [ask](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/9f06332ebd4cfe2577d9eae81aeb58d3662ffccd/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L797) matching loops. This over-subtraction causes the matching loop to terminate prematurely, preventing the order from continuing to match against additional liquidity.\n\nFor Fill-or-Kill orders, this creates a critical failure mode. The FOK validation check\n\n```solidity\n if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n```\n```solidity\nif (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n```\nThis check passes because `newOrder.amount` has been incorrectly reduced to 0, even though dust quote amount remains unfilled. This violates the FOK guarantee that orders either execute completely or fail entirely.\n\nUsers receive fewer base tokens than their quote amount should purchase. Settlement uses the correct (smaller) `quoteDelta` and `baseDelta` values, but the user's order is marked as fully filled despite only partial execution.\n\n\nConsider a bid fill order with:\n\n- `amountIsBase = false`\n- `lotSizeInBase = 1e18`\n- `price = 1e18` (normalized)\n- `remaining taker.amount = 2.5e18` (2.5 quote units)\n- `maker base = 3e18`\n\nThe calculation proceeds as:\n\n1. `potential_base = getBaseTokenAmount(price, 2.5e18) = 2.5e18`\n2. `matchedBase = min(2.5e18, 3e18) = 2.5e18`\n3. `baseDelta = floor(2.5e18 / 1e18) * 1e18 = 2e18` (lot-size flooring)\n4. `quoteDelta = getQuoteTokenAmount(price, 2e18) = 2e18`\n5. Since `baseDelta (2e18) != matchedBase (2.5e18), matchedAmount = takerOrder.amount = 2.5e18`\n\nThe order amount is reduced by 2.5 units, but only 2 units worth of base tokens are actually traded, resulting in a 20% loss of expected value.\n\nThis bug affects all quote-denominated fill orders when lot-size constraints are present, which is a core feature as evidenced by test coverage in .\n\n## Recommendation\nFix the `matchedAmount` calculation for quote-denominated orders\n```solidity\n// Current (incorrect) logic:  \nmatchData.matchedAmount = matchData.baseDelta != matchedBase ? takerOrder.amount : matchData.quoteDelta;  \n  \n// Recommended fix:  \nmatchData.matchedAmount = amountIsBase ? matchData.baseDelta : matchData.quoteDelta;\n```\nThis ensures that for quote-denominated orders (`!amountIsBase`), only the actual quote amount consumed (`quoteDelta`) is subtracted from the remaining order amount, allowing the matching loop to continue processing any remaining quote dust and properly triggering FOK failures when appropriate.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {Side} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n    }\n\n    /// @dev PoC demonstrating significant precision loss vulnerability\n    \n    /// @dev Real-world PoC demonstrating the quote-denominated fill order bug\n    /// This test sets a meaningful lot size to trigger the bug condition\n    function testWorldQuoteDenominatedFillOrderBug() public {\n        // Setup users\n        address maker = makeAddr(\"realMaker\");\n        address taker = makeAddr(\"realTaker\");\n\n        // Set a lot size that will cause flooring - this is key to triggering the bug\n        uint256 lotSize = 1e18; // 1 ether lot size\n        vm.prank(address(clobManager));\n        clob.setLotSizeInBase(lotSize);\n\n        // Create the exact scenario from the bug description:\n        // - lotSizeInBase = 1e18\n        // - price = 1e18 (normalized)\n        // - remaining taker.amount = 2.5e18 (2.5 quote units)\n        // - maker base = 3e18\n\n        uint256 price = 1e18; // 1:1 price ratio\n        uint256 makerBaseAmount = 3e18; // Maker has 3 base tokens\n        uint256 takerQuoteAmount = 2500000000000000000; // Taker wants to spend 2.5 quote tokens\n\n        // Setup tokens\n        baseToken.mint(maker, makerBaseAmount);\n        quoteToken.mint(taker, takerQuoteAmount);\n\n        // Approve and deposit\n        vm.prank(maker);\n        baseToken.approve(address(accountManager), makerBaseAmount);\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(accountManager), takerQuoteAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(maker);\n        accountManager.deposit(maker, address(baseToken), makerBaseAmount);\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        accountManager.deposit(taker, address(quoteToken), takerQuoteAmount);\n\n        // Maker places a sell limit order\n        vm.prank(maker);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(\n            maker,\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase: makerBaseAmount,\n                clientOrderId: 0,\n                price: price,\n                cancelTimestamp: type(uint32).max,\n                side: Side.SELL,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Check balances before\n        uint256 takerQuoteBefore = accountManager.getAccountBalance(taker, address(quoteToken));\n        uint256 takerBaseBefore = accountManager.getAccountBalance(taker, address(baseToken));\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Quote-Denominated Fill Order Bug Demo ===\");\n        console.log(\"Lot size:\", lotSize);\n        console.log(\"Price:\", price);\n        console.log(\"Taker quote amount:\", takerQuoteAmount);\n        console.log(\"Taker quote before:\", takerQuoteBefore);\n        console.log(\"Taker base before:\", takerBaseBefore);\n\n        // Calculate expected behavior according to bug description:\n        // potential_base = getBaseTokenAmount(price, 2.5e18) = 2.5e18\n        // matchedBase = min(2.5e18, 3e18) = 2.5e18\n        // baseDelta = floor(2.5e18 / 1e18) * 1e18 = 2e18 (lot-size flooring)\n        // quoteDelta = getQuoteTokenAmount(price, 2e18) = 2e18\n        // Since baseDelta (2e18) != matchedBase (2.5e18), matchedAmount = takerOrder.amount = 2.5e18 (BUG!)\n\n        uint256 potentialBase = (takerQuoteAmount * 1e18) / price; // 2.5e18\n        uint256 matchedBase = potentialBase < makerBaseAmount ? potentialBase : makerBaseAmount; // 2.5e18\n        uint256 baseDelta = (matchedBase / lotSize) * lotSize; // 2e18 (floored)\n        uint256 quoteDelta = (baseDelta * price) / 1e18; // 2e18\n\n        console.log(\"Expected potential base:\", potentialBase);\n        console.log(\"Expected matched base:\", matchedBase);\n        console.log(\"Expected base delta (floored):\", baseDelta);\n        console.log(\"Expected quote delta:\", quoteDelta);\n        console.log(\"Bug condition (baseDelta != matchedBase):\", baseDelta != matchedBase);\n\n        // Taker places a quote-denominated fill order (this triggers the bug)\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        ICLOB.PostFillOrderResult memory result = clob.postFillOrder(\n            taker,\n            ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs({\n                amount: takerQuoteAmount, // 2.5 quote tokens\n                priceLimit: price, // Price limit\n                amountIsBase: false, // Quote-denominated (triggers the bug path)\n                side: Side.BUY,\n                fillOrderType: ICLOB.FillOrderType.IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Check balances after\n        uint256 takerQuoteAfter = accountManager.getAccountBalance(taker, address(quoteToken));\n        uint256 takerBaseAfter = accountManager.getAccountBalance(taker, address(baseToken));\n\n        // Calculate actual amounts\n        uint256 baseReceived = takerBaseAfter - takerBaseBefore;\n        uint256 quoteSpent = takerQuoteBefore - takerQuoteAfter;\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Actual Results ===\");\n        console.log(\"Quote spent by taker:\", quoteSpent);\n        console.log(\"Base received by taker:\", baseReceived);\n        console.log(\"Fill result quote traded:\", result.quoteTokenAmountTraded);\n        console.log(\"Fill result base traded:\", result.baseTokenAmountTraded);\n\n        // The bug: Due to lot-size flooring, only 2e18 base should be traded\n        // But the matchedAmount calculation incorrectly uses the full 2.5e18 quote amount\n        // This causes the order to appear fully filled when it should have 0.5e18 quote remaining\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Bug Analysis ===\");\n        console.log(\"Expected base received (after lot flooring):\", baseDelta);\n        console.log(\"Expected quote spent (for floored base):\", quoteDelta);\n        console.log(\"Actual base received:\", baseReceived);\n        console.log(\"Actual quote spent:\", quoteSpent);\n\n        // Account for taker fees in the assertion\n        uint256 expectedBaseAfterFees = baseDelta - (baseDelta * 50) / 100000; // 0.05% taker fee\n\n        // The key bug demonstration: lot-size flooring occurred correctly\n        assertEq(quoteSpent, quoteDelta, \"Should spend corresponding quote amount\");\n        assertApproxEqRel(baseReceived, expectedBaseAfterFees, 1e15, \"Should receive floored base amount minus fees\");\n        assertLt(baseReceived, potentialBase, \"Should receive less than potential due to flooring\");\n        assertLt(quoteSpent, takerQuoteAmount, \"Should spend less than intended due to flooring\");\n\n        // Most importantly: verify the bug condition was triggered\n        assertTrue(baseDelta != matchedBase, \"Bug condition: baseDelta != matchedBase should be true\");\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Economic Impact ===\");\n        console.log(\"Base tokens lost to lot-size flooring:\", potentialBase - baseReceived);\n        console.log(\"Quote tokens not utilized:\", takerQuoteAmount - quoteSpent);\n\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nLogs\n\n```bash\nLogs:\n  \n=== Quote-Denominated Fill Order Bug Demo ===\n  Lot size: 1000000000000000000\n  Price: 1000000000000000000\n  Taker quote amount: 2500000000000000000\n  Taker quote before: 2500000000000000000\n  Taker base before: 0\n  Expected potential base: 2500000000000000000\n  Expected matched base: 2500000000000000000\n  Expected base delta (floored): 2000000000000000000\n  Expected quote delta: 2000000000000000000\n  Bug condition (baseDelta != matchedBase): true\n  \n=== Actual Results ===\n  Quote spent by taker: 2000000000000000000\n  Base received by taker: 1999000000000000000\n  Fill result quote traded: -2000000000000000000\n  Fill result base traded: 2000000000000000000\n  \n=== Bug Analysis ===\n  Expected base received (after lot flooring): 2000000000000000000\n  Expected quote spent (for floored base): 2000000000000000000\n  Actual base received: 1999000000000000000\n  Actual quote spent: 2000000000000000000\n  \n=== Economic Impact ===\n  Base tokens lost to lot-size flooring: 501000000000000000\n  Quote tokens not utilized: 500000000000000000\n```",
